From: PowOS
Subject: dma-buf: sync_file import/export build flat fences (upstream dma_fence_unwrap_merge) - fixes reboots at game close

Fix for 0004. Its dma_buf_resv_fence wrapped every fence on the buffer in a NEW dma_fence_array - including the
exclusive fence a previous IMPORT_SYNC_FILE(WRITE) had set, which was already such an array - and kept signaled
fences. Mesa's Vulkan WSI imports a write fence for every frame it presents, so a game's swapchain dma-buf carried a
fence array nested one level deeper per frame shown. Freeing the buffer (the game or Steam closing) released that
nest recursively, dma_fence_array_release -> dma_fence_put -> dma_fence_array_release ..., once per frame, on the
16 KB kernel stack: the phone rebooted at every game close (2026-10-23 10:33, 10:53, 10:58, 11:14; boot reason
"reboot", pstore empty).

Now the fences go through upstream's __dma_fence_unwrap_merge, which this android13-5.15 tree already has (Android
backported dma-fence-unwrap; sync_file_merge uses it): arrays and chains unwrapped, signaled fences dropped, one
fence per context (the later one), the single remaining fence returned as itself, else one flat array, else a
signaled stub. A buffer's fence is at most one array of unsignaled fences, one per context, whatever the frame count.
KMI: dma-buf.c's static functions only; __dma_fence_unwrap_merge is an existing exported symbol.
